<node id="11124465" title="Re: How can I sort my array numerically on part of the string?" created="2020-12-01 13:09:17" updated="2020-12-01 13:09:17" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="170442">jdporter</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">
&lt;p&gt;
You're in luck &amp;mdash; the numeric part is at the beginning of the string.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;code&gt;
my @list = ( '1,cat', '2,dog', '22,mouse', '11,eel', '001,elk', '13,mink');

my @sorted = sort { $a &lt;=&gt; $b } @list;
&lt;/code&gt;

&lt;div class="pmsig"&gt;&lt;div class="pmsig-170442"&gt;
I reckon we are the only monastery ever to have a dungeon stuffed with 16[523120|,]000 zombies.
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</doctext>
